&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to make a serious impact? Millions of people already rely on Calendly, and we’re still in the midst of exciting product growth — it’s a fantastic time to join us. Everything you’ll work on here will accelerate your career to the next level. If you want to learn, grow, and do the best work of your life alongside the best people you’ve ever worked with, then we hope you’ll consider allowing Calendly to be a part of your professional journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A day in the life of a Staff Product Manager at Calendly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This technical product management position will report to the Head of Engineering, Growth and Customer foundations team. We strive to design a seamless product experience that delights our customers. In 2026, Calendly chartered a company-wide initiative to focus on delivering &lt;em&gt;Great Customer Experience&lt;/em&gt; -spanning our Help Center, AI support bot, Automated issue resolution, human support escalations and support engineering. We&#39;re hiring a technical Staff Product Manager to work across Product, Go to Market (GTM) stakeholders, marketing, customer support and multiple engineering squads to address real gaps in taxonomy, measurement, and process. This product manager will own the roadmap end-to-end and turn a set of disconnected efforts into a durable, multi-quarter capability that will drive defined growth, product/business outcomes, and customer satisfaction goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;On a typical day, you will be working on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the strategy, roadmap, and outcomes&lt;/strong&gt; for Calendly’s intelligent customer experience, spanning AI support quality, automated resolution, and human escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Increase automated resolution&lt;/strong&gt; by enabling the Support Agent to accurately answer questions and take actions on behalf of customers, while reserving human support for high-value and complex issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and improve AI quality&lt;/strong&gt;, including answer accuracy, resolution quality, escalation effectiveness, and the failure modes that prevent customers from getting the right outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the measurement and observability layer&lt;/strong&gt; for Agent/Bot Quality Score, automated resolution rate, customer experience cycle time, escalation routing, and customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish and drive adoption of a company-wide “supportability contract”&lt;/strong&gt; so every new Calendly capability is supportable by AI agents, automation, or human support from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the loop between customer issues and R&amp;amp;D&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring recurring bugs, product gaps, and support insights translate into prioritized product and engineering actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead across Product, Engineering, AI/Data, Growth, Monetization, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Support, and Content Operations&lt;/strong&gt; to turn fragmented customer-support efforts into a durable, scalable company capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use customer feedback, support data, and experimentation&lt;/strong&gt; to continuously improve the experience, prioritize investments, and measure progress against clear customer and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we need from you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This hybrid opportunity is open exclusively to candidates currently residing in California who can commute to our San Francisco Bay Area office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 10+ years of varied PM experience across both startups and scaled companies, including time spent building 0-to-1 platforms or capabilities that other internal teams had to adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with AI-powered agents and/or conversational agents. You have relevant experience and deeply understand where these systems actually fail and what moves answer quality, not just the pitch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving cross-functional standards or platform adoption across teams you don&#39;t manage — this role has real influence-without-authority demands from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense grounded in support and/or Customer experience data. Comfortable defining metrics from messy or incomplete data rather than waiting for a clean dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build a bold and ambitious vision for the organization with ability to inspire teams to achieve a bold mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with GTM (support, success, content) and R&amp;amp;D stakeholders simultaneously, ideally in a Business to Customer (B2C) and/or Business to Business (B2B) Software as a Service (SaaS), product-led-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authorized to work lawfully in the United States of America as Calendly does not engage in immigration sponsorship at this time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to make a serious impact? Millions of people already rely on Calendly’s products, and we’re still in the midst of our growth curve — it’s a phenomenal time to join us. Everything you’ll work on here will accelerate your career to the next level. If you want to learn, grow, and do the best work of your life alongside the best people you’ve ever worked with, then we hope you’ll consider allowing Calendly to be a part of your professional career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Hiring Process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Typically, individuals will participate in the following interview process. However, there may be slight nuances given the role and or department we are hiring for. Please keep in mind that individuals can be declined from the position at any stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified individuals will be invited to schedule a phone interview with a member of our recruiting team. This is a great time to ask any initial questions you have about the company or the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Next, we’ll put you in direct contact with your potential manager. You’ll get a chance to learn even more about life at Calendly, the responsibilities within your role, and the qualities needed to succeed here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Then, you will perform an interview exercise, where you can highlight your skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Next, or in parallel, you’ll meet with your potential team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finally, we connect with those you’ve worked with before, to learn more about the impact you can make, the value you bring, and the best way to set you up for success at Calendly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Tier 1 Salary Hiring Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$237,305&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,121 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Tier 2 Salary Hiring Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$217,530&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$275,111 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Tier 3 Salary Hiring Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$197,754&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$250,101 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ranges listed above are the expected annual base salary for this role, subject to change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Calendly takes a number of factors into consideration when determining an employee’s starting salary, including relevant experience, relevant skills sets, interview performance, location/metropolitan area, and internal pay equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one component of Calendly’s total rewards package. All full-time (30 hours/week) employees are also eligible for equity awards, and competitive benefits. Eligible Sales employees also qualify for a Sales Incentive program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Calendly uses the zip code of an employee’s remote work location, or the onsite building location if hybrid, to determine which metropolitan pay range we use. Current geographic zones are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tier 1: San Francisco, CA, San Jose, CA, New York City, NY&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tier 2: Chicago, IL, Austin, TX, Denver, CO, Boston, MA, Washington D.C., Philadelphia, PA, Portland, OR, Seattle, WA, Miami, FL, and all other cities in CA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tier 3: All other locations not in Tier 1 or Tier 2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are an individual with a disability and would like to request a reasonable accommodation as part of the application or recruiting process, please let your Recruiter know when first connecting with them. Calendly is registered as an employer in many, but not all, states. If you are located in Alaska, Delaware, Hawaii, Idaho, Iowa, Montana, Nebraska, North Dakota, Rhode Island, South Dakota, and West Virginia, you will not be eligible for employment. Note that all individual roles will specify location eligibility.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All candidates can find our Candidate Privacy Statement&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UarTnO5b7rIEKowqiyRvw1Zz81mROP7tq-NR7sCmhBM/edit&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidates residing in California may visit our Notice at Collection for California Candidates here:&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1d58_uJ1S0ti5jMlekLhXRswLfJAdw0A6/edit#bookmark=id.gjdgxs&quot;&gt; Notice at Collection&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require occasional travel for company events, team collaboration, or offsites.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to make a serious impact? Millions of people already rely on Calendly, and we’re still in the midst of exciting product growth — it’s a fantastic time to join us. Everything you’ll work on here will accelerate your career to the next level. If you want to learn, grow, and do the best work of your life alongside the best people you’ve ever worked with, then we hope you’ll consider allowing Calendly to be a part of your professional journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager, Meetings&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll own and evolve this category-defining experience—making scheduling simpler, expanding proven capabilities into new workflows and customer segments, and helping customers get more value across the meeting lifecycle.&lt;br&gt;Millions of people rely on Calendly every day to schedule and manage their meetings, with thousands more joining daily. Meetings is the foundation of the Calendly experience and the core of our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape the future of a scaled product used by millions while balancing what makes Calendly successful today with where meetings need to go next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*This is a hybrid position located in the Bay Area, with an expectation to work from our San Francisco office two (2) days per week.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the Meetings strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify the highest-leverage customer and business opportunities across Calendly’s core scheduling experience and translate them into a clear product strategy and roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make scheduling effortless:&lt;/strong&gt; Simplify mature workflows, remove friction, and make sophisticated scheduling capabilities intuitive and easy to adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive growth of the core business:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to improve activation, engagement, retention, and monetization across individual and team customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand proven capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Scale underused and emerging capabilities into new customer segments, workflows, and use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the future of Meetings:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop a strong point of view on how changing customer behaviors and AI will reshape scheduling and meeting management, and translate that into product investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead through influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Align Engineering, Design, Data, Research, Marketing, Sales, and senior leadership around product decisions, priorities, and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own outcomes, not output:&lt;/strong&gt; Define the OKRs and KPIs that matter, use customer insights and data to make decisions, and continuously iterate based on results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the product bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring strong product judgment and customer empathy to one of Calendly’s most important product surfaces while preserving the simplicity customers expect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8–10 years of product management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including significant ownership of a scaled, mature product at a product-driven B2B or B2C SaaS company; experience at a well-scaled company (Series D+) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting product strategy and driving measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience evolving a &lt;strong&gt;core product at scale&lt;/strong&gt; and materially improving metrics such as activation, adoption, engagement, retention, revenue, or customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional &lt;strong&gt;product sense and customer empathy&lt;/strong&gt;, with experience turning complex workflows into simple, intuitive customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with &lt;strong&gt;product-led growth&lt;/strong&gt;, including self-serve acquisition, activation, virality, engagement, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for both &lt;strong&gt;individual users and organizations&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally in collaboration, productivity, scheduling, or work management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI in product development and a strong point of view on how AI can improve customer workflows; experience shipping AI-powered features is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment and the ability to combine quantitative data, customer research, and product intuition to make difficult prioritization decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence senior leaders and cross-functional teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguity, challenging assumptions, making clear tradeoffs, and moving quickly when decisions are reversible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to partner effectively with Engineering on platform capabilities, integrations, APIs, and architecture. An engineering background is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to work from our San Francisco office two (2) days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authorized to work lawfully in the United States of America; Calendly does not provide immigration sponsorship for this role at this time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help Calendly strengthen and evolve the product that brought millions of customers to us in the first place: &lt;strong&gt;making scheduling effortless while expanding the value customers get from Calendly before, during, and after every meeting.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Tier 1 Salary Hiring Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$237,305&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$300,121 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ranges listed above are the expected annual base salary for this role, subject to change.&lt;/p&gt;
